  "kind": "build",
  "title": "# Build: molly-multi-instance-tabs (FABLE: touches xlayout@1 / windows / dock contracts) ## What Br…",
  "asked": "# Build: molly-multi-instance-tabs (FABLE: touches xlayout@1 / windows / dock contracts) ## What Brett said (verbatim, Nov 4 2026, voice) In Molly's xLayout IDE mode: \"How do I make a new tab in Molly?\" ... (there's no + button) ... \"Need to be able to add a tab so I can have multiple instances.\" Also: \"How do I reset the layout? Because I run it IDE style and I made a bunch of tabs.\" He couldn't find Reset layout (it exists as the workspace action `layout-reset` in src/axf/libs/workspace, but he can't see it). Book to a free named agent. ## Do - **New tab (+)** at the end of every tab group in Molly (and the same shared tab component anywhere else). It opens a picker: AmberX / axHub / Console / any Molly plugin, plus 'Duplicate this tab'. - **Multiple instances of the same app**: each instance is its own tab and its own iframe/session (instance id in the tab spec; xlayout@1 / windows engine allow the same app more than once). The console instance must connect as its own console client so Amber can target it. Tabs are labelled 'Console 2', etc., renameable, and remembered across reloads. - Right-click a tab: New tab / Duplicate / Rename / Close / Close others / Move to pane / Pop out to window. - **Reset layout made findable**: in the app menu under View / Layout, in right-click on any pane or tab bar, in xLayout settings, and as a voice/console control. It confirms first and is undoable. - Respect the pane limit and dock rules, and coordinate with tab-group-assets (shared tab-group@1) via THREADS. - PORTING.md (Android deferred), tests, UI Review shots (non-blocking), PR, auto-land, redeploy Molly. Report in _claude/builds/reports/. Commits clean. ## ADDENDUM 1 (Brett, voice, Nov 4) \"Any screen or any UI whatsoever can be dragged.\" - Every screen, plugin view, panel, dialog and app instance can be dragged by its title or tab: into another tab group, into a new pane (drop zones on any edge), out to a floating window, or back. Uses the shared dock engine (dock@1) so it works the same in Molly, the console, AmberX and axHub web. - Phone: long-press then drag. Drop targets are highlighted. Undo after every drop. - Make it a rule in RULES.md / PORTING.md: no UI surface is fixed in place. List any surface you couldn't make draggable in the report. Watch live: Brett can watch the screen you are changing hot-render in the console. Whenever you start work on a screen or element, run `node framework/cli/axf.mjs focus <app> [route] [css-selector] --note \"<what you are changing>\"` (apps: console-web, axhub-web, amberx-droid, walkthrough-studio, demo, framework, console, axhub-android, voicevault). Agent cap: heavy steps (pnpm/npm/vite builds, docker node:22 test runs, Playwright) share a VPS-wide lock. Run each one as `node /opt/axf/deploy/../framework/cli/agent-slots.mjs heavy -- <command>` so only a few run at once. Model switches (Brett, Nov 3 2026): a downgrade (e.g. Fable → Opus) is fine. An UPGRADE (e.g. Opus → Fable) needs Brett's approval: when you reach one, run `node apps/console-web/plugins/build-orchestrator/orchestrator.mjs request-upgrade <id> <phase>`, ask once, and stop. Never approve a model switch upgrade yourself (no `act approve` on an upgrade), never relaunch on a higher model.",
